            "question": "Do I need a permit for a glass railing in Houston if there is no zoning?",
            "answer": "<p>Usually, yes. Zoning controls land use; the building code controls construction. Houston applies the 2021 IRC and IBC with local amendments. A new deck, rooftop deck, balcony or pool barrier normally needs a building permit from the Houston Permitting Center and an inspection. Replacing an existing railing is sometimes treated differently, so ask before you order. West University, Bellaire and the Memorial villages have their own building departments.</p>",
