          "settings": {
            "question": "How high does a glass railing need to be on a Houston townhome rooftop deck?",
            "answer": "<p>For a single-family townhome, the code sets a 36\" minimum guard height, and the 33.6\" panel in a 6\" spigot gives 36\". Some owners prefer the 39.6\" panel, a 42\" railing, three stories up. Spigots top-mount to the framing or side-mount to the fascia; our engineering documents cover both on wood and concrete. Send photos of the roof edge with your quote request; membranes and parapets change the attachment plan.</p>",
            "pages": ""
